    "title": "20-year-old Freedom man dead after crash involving motorcycle and SUV - NewsBreak",
    "text": "CENTER, Wis. (WFRV) – A 20-year-old Freedom man died after crashing into an SUV in Outagamie County on Wednesday afternoon. According to the Outagamie County Sheriff’s Office, deputies responded around 3 p.m. to a crash report involving an SUV and a motorcycle near the intersection of Meade Street and Mackville Road in Center. Preliminary investigation details indicate that the motorcyclist was heading southbound on Meade when they struck an SUV turning onto Meade Street from private property. The motorcyclist was identified as a 20-year-old Freedom man, and he died from his injuries at the scene. The SUV driver, a 26-year-old Grand Chute woman, was unharmed. Alcohol is not believed to have been a factor in the crash. Meade Street was closed for about 4.5 hours as deputies and officials were on the scene. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WFRV Local 5 - Green Bay, Appleton.",
